"""Independent full original-field readings, frozen before candidate inspection."""
NOTES = {}
def note(number, language, text, collection='bukhari'):
    key=('deenhindi-'+collection+':'+number,language)
    assert key not in NOTES
    NOTES[key]=text

note('2390','hi','Abu Hurayrah through the supplied home-transmission frame reports the creditor’s demand, the companions’ attempted punishment, and the Messenger’s right-to-speak and better-camel repayment replies. The parenthetic camel-that-he-loaned relation identifies the actual comparison object and remains meaningful report scope. No missing identity is supplied.')
note('2390','ur','The complete creditor/camel dialogue is supplied through Abu Hurayrah. Retain the parenthetic loan relation in the comparison, but the final sentence declaring agreement between hadith and chapter is compiler apparatus, not another report clause. Preserve its exact words as context.')
note('2394','hi','Jabir supplies the mosque visit, two-rakah instruction and repayment with extra. Misar’s own I-think timing statement materially qualifies the time and should remain a separately attributed transmitter voice in this same report family. The parenthetic explanation that he visited then repeats the already supplied visit/time relation and can remain context.')
note('2394','ur','The own Urdu supplies Jabir’s visit and repayment, with Misar’s explicit uncertainty about mention of the forenoon. Preserve that named uncertainty, not as Prophetic speech. The parenthetic that-he-presented-himself-at-that-time repeats the complete timing/visit statement and is explanatory context.')
note('2395','hi','Jabir reports his father’s death, creditor refusal, the Messenger’s proposed fruit settlement and later visit/blessing, and payment with fruit left over. The father-name parenthesis is an appositional identity label; the supplied father relation already remains. All actual refusal, future visit and remainder wording stays exact.')
note('2395','ur','This full own report reaches Jabir and gives the father’s debt, creditor refusal and garden blessing/repayment outcome. Abdullah in parentheses is a separate identity gloss, not a missing event. Retain the complete actual sequence and the Urdu punctuation without importing anything from Hindi.')
note('2401','hi','Abu Hurayrah reports the creditor’s harsh demand and the attempted chastisement, followed by the Messenger’s actual leave-him/right-holder reply. The complete own short body is finite and needs no omitted camel account from another occurrence.')
note('2401','ur','The complete Urdu gives the harsh demand, companions’ wish to chastise and actual leave-him reply. It is a source-bound Prophetic encounter report with its own abbreviated extent; no continuation is inferred.')
note('2405','hi','I read both complete accounts: Jabir’s father/debt/date settlement, then the separately timed expedition/camel-sale/marriage/homecoming account. Retain both my-father relations and the different-occasion qualifier, which provide actual participant and occasion scope. The camel right-to-ride, widow/children purpose and returning price/camel/share are supplied; keep two report families without merging this ID with 2406.')
note('2405','ur','The own Urdu contains two full Jabir narratives, each read independently: date-debt settlement and the later campaign/camel/marriage encounter. Its repeated my-father relations and separate-occasion phrase are meaningful source scope. Preserve exact own wording, named date kinds and final price/camel/booty-share sequence; retain the source identity even where another row has equal text.')
note('2406','hi','I separately read this occurrence’s full Hindi, even though its complete text equals 2405 Hindi. It contains the date-debt report and distinct campaign/camel/marriage report. Retain the two actual family/occasion qualifications, all supplied dialogue and final three-part gift outcome; do not collapse its provider identity into 2405.')
note('2406','ur','This own Urdu was read in full as a distinct source occurrence. The two actual Jabir accounts and the parenthetic my-father/different-occasion scope are supplied. Equal wording with 2405 establishes no license to merge IDs or skip this reading; no language or source repair is added.')
note('2407','hi','The source route literally names Umar after Abdullah ibn Dinar, followed by the unnamed man’s deception complaint, the Messenger’s no-deception formula and the man’s later practice. Keep that printed name and complete report; do not silently change it to Ibn Umar using an external version.')
note('2407','ur','The own Urdu expressly prints Umar and the actual sale/deception complaint and response, ending with the man’s practice. Preserve the literal route and complete finite body. There is no source authority here for a cross-edition narrator correction.')
note('2413','hi','Anas reports the injured girl, naming inquiry, head indication, confession and historical punishment. The remaining-life parenthesis supplies the victim’s actual condition at questioning; the that-yes phrase supplies the meaning of the otherwise unspecified head gesture. Retain both narrative qualifications, with the violent events as a reported historical account.')
note('2413','ur','The complete Urdu recounts the girl’s condition, question, affirmative head gesture, confession and reported punishment. Both the some-life-remained condition and that-yes answer are substantive supplied scene/response clauses, not redundant lexical synonyms. No unnamed identity is added.')
note('2415','hi','Jabir supplies the man’s freeing of a slave, absence of other property, the Messenger’s reversal and Nuaim ibn Nahham’s purchase. The absence-of-other-property clause is actual limiting narrative context and remains part of this own finite report; no broader ruling or external identification is substituted.')
note('2415','ur','The own Urdu gives the full freeing/no-other-property/reversal/purchase sequence through Jabir. Retain the printed buyer name and condition without filling a different canonical narration or expanding the statement beyond its source wording.')
note('2418','hi','Kab’s debt dispute with Ibn Abi Hadrad is a complete source report: loud voices, curtain lifted, half-remission gesture, acceptance and order to repay. All amount, action and distinct speaker links are supplied and retained. No compiler appendix is present.')
note('2418','ur','The Urdu independently supplies Kab’s demand, the Messenger’s intervention, the exact half-remission and Ibn Abi Hadrad repayment order. Preserve the full own sequence, named roles and source chain. Its completeness does not establish that other language fields were read.')
note('2423','hi','Abu Hurayrah reports the sending of mounted men to Najd, capture of Thumamah from Banu Hanifah and binding to the mosque pillar. This is an actual finite abbreviated event report; its unprinted later story must not be supplied.')
note('2423','ur','The own Urdu supplies the mission/capture/binding events with Thumamah ibn Athal as printed. Admit only this actual short account under its own source attribution; no release/conversion or other unseen continuation belongs to it.')
note('2425','hi','Khabbab’s debt dialogue contains his refusal to deny Muhammad and the opponent’s actual claim about repayment after death/revival. The kafir apposition and repeated second-life gloss are explanation. Retain the actual reported revelation quotation and its supplied Hindi rendering as embedded source content with a distinct qualified voice; the final to-end-of-verse phrase is an omitted-continuation pointer, not additional quotation.')
note('2425','ur','I read the entire Khabbab/As ibn Wail debt exchange, the actual Arabic verse excerpt and supplied Urdu rendering. Kafir and second-life parenthetical glosses are separate explanation; final akhir-ayat-tak is apparatus. Preserve actual dialogue and recitation/rendering, without supplying the missing verse continuation or calling the opponent’s words the Prophet’s words.')
note('2427','hi','Zayd ibn Khalid’s reported lost-property dialogue supplies an actual conditional whose then-return-the-property predicate appears in parentheses and must remain. The owner gloss after brother and walking-function explanation after hooves are explanatory labels rather than missing commands. Keep the source’s full alternatives, one-year announcement, face change and camel self-care clauses.')
note('2427','ur','The complete own Urdu supplies lost-property, sheep and camel questions. Retain the parenthetic return-it command as the actual condition’s consequence. My initial boundary judgment puts malik and the explanatory with-which-it-will-walk aside in context, leaving all supplied commands, alternatives and animal capacities exact; later candidate comparison may refine this explicitly.')
note('2431','hi','Anas reports the Messenger seeing a date on the road and the actual conditional that he would eat it were it not possibly charity. Keep the complete own short report, including the condition and its uncertainty; no missing ownership claim is inferred.')
note('2431','ur','The own Urdu contains the complete date/possible-charity conditional saying through Anas. All actual wording is finite report content; the source does not identify the date’s owner or certainty of charity, so neither is added.')
note('2437.2','hi','The initial above-hadith pointer is apparatus, but the later meeting in Mecca and explicit memory uncertainty between one and three years are actual supplied finite statements. Preserve Salamah/Ubay/Kaab as printed and qualify the I/he antecedents rather than borrowing a known transmission chain. The uncertainty is not an unqualified Prophetic instruction.')
note('2437.2','ur','I read the own short added-route account: pointer to the earlier hadith followed by actual later meeting and one-versus-three-year memory limitation. Preserve the uncertain voice and source wording without canonical correction of the printed Kaab link; the material doubt remains within the source report family.')
note('2439','hi','Abu Bakr’s complete shepherd/milk/cooling/serving account is supplied after two chains. The explicit second-chain label is apparatus; the migration-to-Medina temporal phrase supplies the actual narrative occasion and stays. Preserve the unnamed Qurayshi owner, cleaning actions, cooling sequence and Abu Bakr’s final satisfaction without adding outside identities.')
note('2439','ur','The own Urdu fully recounts Abu Bakr’s encounter and milk presentation. Retain the migration occasion and complete requests/actions and outcome. Move only the explicit second-chain label to transmission context; both actual chains remain source framing without an invented additional occurrence.')
note('2450','hi','Aisha supplies an attributed finite explanation of a wife’s relinquishing her right when her husband wishes separation, attached to an actual verse excerpt and Hindi meaning. This is an expanded Companion saying, not anonymous compiler explanation or direct Prophetic speech. The parenthetic Quran-verse label is apparatus; the supplied recitation, rendering and statement stay exact.')
note('2450','ur','The own Urdu explicitly attributes the wife/right/separation explanation to Aisha and includes its actual verse excerpt and Urdu rendering. Preserve those as the numbered Companion saying with qualified embedded recitation, while the parenthetic Quran-verse label is context. Do not substitute a canonical external verse number.')
note('2460','hi','Aisha reports Hind’s question about Abu Sufyan’s miserliness and feeding her children, and the Messenger’s customary-amount reply. The parenthetic husband relation supplies actual participant scope not otherwise explicit and should remain, without expanding the permission into an unqualified present instruction.')
note('2460','ur','The complete own Urdu supplies Hind’s complaint, the husband relation and children-feeding question with the customary-condition reply. Retain the spouse relation as meaningful relational scope; no identity or legal rule is borrowed from a sibling or an external edition.')
note('2461','hi','Uqbah reports the group’s hospitality question and the Messenger’s conditional reply. The some-times qualifier limits the claim about inhospitable hosts and remains material. Keep the conditions and right-of-hospitality object, as source-reported speech rather than a newly generalized instruction.')
note('2461','ur','The own Urdu has the actual delegation/occasion question and conditional acceptance-or-right-recovery reply. The some-occasions parenthesis narrows the narrative and must remain; all actual conditions and addressees stay as printed.')
note('2462','hi','Umar through Ibn Abbas reports the Ansar gathering after the Prophet’s death and his own request to Abu Bakr to go there. This finite historical Companion report is not a Prophetic saying. The second-chain label is apparatus; retain the exact source scene and participants without adding the unprinted later political account.')
note('2462','ur','The own Urdu supplies Umar’s actual after-death gathering and going-to-Saqifah account through Ibn Abbas. Preserve the named speaker and historical scope, while the explicit second-chain label stays context. Do not add a later result or an identity merge with other occurrences.')
note('2464','hi','Anas reports serving date wine, the prohibition announcement, Abu Talhah’s order, the spilling and people’s concern, followed by actual verse wording and its supplied rendering. The parenthetic revelation occasion and immediate-hearing relation give substantive chronology and remain. The final to-end-of-verse pointer is context; the actual recitation/translation must not be discarded with it.')
note('2464','ur','I read the entire own Anas account and embedded Arabic/Urdu verse excerpt. Retain the supplied revelation timing and hearing-then-command sequence, the people’s expressed concern and actual verse/meaning. Only the final akhir-ayat-tak continuation instruction is apparatus; preserve damaged closing punctuation rather than completing the verse.')
note('2467','hi','Usamah reports the Messenger’s elevated view and actual comparison of coming trials to rain. The soon qualifier materially narrows the future statement, including its malformed leading quote, and remains literal. No identification of future people/events is invented.')
note('2467','ur','The full own Urdu supplies the elevated-house scene and the actual coming-trials comparison. Retain anqarib as the source’s real temporal limit, not a redundant synonym, and avoid asserting what outside event fulfills it.')
note('2376','hi','Numan ibn Bashir’s own Hindi contains a damaged gift/visit link: ghulam is misspelled and only the tail of an honorific survives before the visit. The father, gift, intended witnessing and actual question/no/return-it response are supplied. Preserve every defect and qualify the authoritative addressee by the source’s honorific pronouns rather than inserting the explicit Prophet name from Urdu.',collection='ibnmajah')
note('2376','ur','The own Urdu explicitly names the Prophet in Numan’s father/gift/witnessing account, followed by the all-sons question, no-answer and take-it-back reply. This complete field supports its own direct attribution; it does not repair the damaged Hindi link.',collection='ibnmajah')

assert len(NOTES)==46
